.git
.github
# Every local virtualenv, not just `.venv`. A local `docker build` uses the WORKING TREE
# as its context, so a dev venv lands in the image via `COPY . .` — and it brings its own
# CVEs with it. Building this repo locally baked `.venv-mineru` (the arm64 MinerU pilot
# venv) into /app and added 13 Trivy findings that have nothing to do with the service:
# gradio, transformers, starlette, aiohttp, pypdf. CI never saw them because its context
# is a clean git checkout, which is exactly what makes this the kind of gap that only
# shows up when someone builds by hand.
.venv*
.env
.env.*
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.ruff_cache
*.egg-info
# Index artifacts are NOT baked — they come from the /data volume mount.
data/
# Stage-1 extraction output is served from the /docs mount (dev) or S3 (prod), never baked.
out/
model-cache/
docs/
*.md
!README.md
# Below: extra excludes for the SERVICE image only (this file overrides the
# base .dockerignore for `docker build -f Dockerfile`, it does not merge with
# it — that's why everything above is duplicated from .dockerignore rather
# than just appended). The service only ever IMPORTS from src/ (see
# pyproject.toml: packages = ["src/aosphere_core_index"]), so none of this is
# reachable from the running app.
#
# scripts/ is NOT excluded, and must not be. It is not imported, but it is
# EXECUTED out of this image: deploy/promotion-job.yaml runs
# `python scripts/promote_run.py` on the API image by design, and
# POST /api/admin/entity-reindex spawns scripts/sync_atlas_search.py. Excluding
# it here made `docker build -f Dockerfile` drop both from the context, and the
# promotion Job died on "can't open file '/app/scripts/promote_run.py'". The
# cache win that exclusion was after is kept instead by COPYing scripts/ in the
# LAST layer of the Dockerfile, after the pip install and the model warmups.
tests/
test/
test pdf/
output/
